# Meeting 3 - Data Analyst Project

Wed, 26 Aug 26

### Repo Rename Trigger

- Samir requested a name change to the shared repo
- Rename initially failed; refreshing the page resolved it
- Renaming broke existing clones for the team, requiring everyone to re-clone

### Re-clone Errors and Debugging

- Root cause: renamed repo path no longer matched local folder references
- Common error: “cannot clone to non-empty folder”
  - Fix: delete the existing local folder entirely, then re-clone into an empty directory
- Secondary issue: trailing space in the folder/path name
  - Windows file systems do not allow trailing spaces in paths
  - Samir removed the trailing space, committed, and pushed: resolved the errors

### Workarounds Attempted

- Manual git status and git restore --source HEAD tried
- GitHub Desktop “add existing repository from local device” attempted
- Downloading the ZIP directly from GitHub page worked as a fallback
- Mac users were unaffected; errors were Windows-specific

### Resolution

- Samir deleted the placeholder folder with the trailing space and re-pushed
- No errors after the push; team pulled successfully from main
- Repo size noted as ballooning: flagged for cleanup after the session

### Takeaway

- A simple rename cascaded into path and file system errors across Windows machines
- Troubleshooting framed as realistic interview prep: debugging under pressure is normal day-to-day work

